		},
		sections={
			{id=2551,title="Nemesis Strike",body="Anraphet strikes his current target, inflicting Shadow damage equal to $75604s1% of his normal melee attack and $75603s1 Shadow damage every $75603t1 seconds for $75603d."},
			{id=2552,title="Alpha Beams",body="Anraphet begins to channel Alpha Beams at a random player, inflicting $76956s1 Shadow damage to players within $76956A1 yards of the target's location every $76912t1 second for $76912d.$[!2,4\n\nIn Heroic Difficulty the shadowy area of an Alpha Beam persists and inflicts damage for the remainder of the fight.$]"},
			{id=2553,title="Omega Stance",body="Anraphet assumes his Omega Stance, inflicting $75623s1 Shadow damage on all enemy targets every $75622t1 second for $75622d. Omega Stance also reduces the movement speed of enemies by $75623s2% for $75623d."},
			{id=2554,title="Crumbling Ruin",body="After using either Alpha Beams or Omega Stance, Anraphet casts Crumbling Ruin. This ability decreases the maximum health of all enemies by $75609s1%, and stacks up to 10 times."},
		},
	},
	[127]={
		encounterID=127,
		instanceID=70,
		order=4,
		name="Isiset, Construct of Magic",
		lore="Isiset serves to regulate the arcane energies contained within, and produced by, the Halls of Origination. Legend has it that this construct has become enraptured with her own arcane mastery and the perfection with which it seemingly endows her.",
		dungeonEncounterID=1077,
		uiMapID=299,
		pin={x=0.3104,y=0.5},
		difficultyIDs={1,2},
		npcIDs={39587},
		displayIDs={33465},
		loot={
			{itemID=157609,diffs={},faction=-1},
			{itemID=56414,diffs={},faction=-1},
			{itemID=56413,diffs={},faction=-1},
			{itemID=56412,diffs={},faction=-1},
			{itemID=56416,diffs={},faction=-1},
			{itemID=56415,diffs={},faction=-1},
		},
		sections={
			{id=2555,title="Supernova",body="Isiset unleashes a supernova, inflicting $76670s1 Arcane damage and confusing any player who faces her for $74137d."},
			{id=2556,title="Mirror Images",body="When Isiset's remaining health reaches 66%, she splits into three separate creatures. Each of the creatures represents one of her three main abilities. Killing one of the three images prevents her from using that image's ability for the rest of the encounter, but the other two abilities are empowered.\n\nWhen Isiset's remaining health reaches 33%, she again splits but into two separate creatures. These two creatures cast and correspond to her two remaining abilities. Killing one of these two images prevents her from using that image's ability for the rest of the encounter, but the sole remaining ability is further empowered."},
			{id=2557,title="Astral Rain",body="Killing this Mirror Image prevents Isiset from casting Astral Rain."},
			{id=2558,title="Celestial Call",body="Killing this Mirror Image prevents Isiset from casting Celestial Call."},
			{id=2559,title="Veil of Sky",body="Killing this Mirror Image prevents Isiset from casting Veil of Sky."},
			{id=2560,title="Astral Rain",body="Isiset summons a shower of stars, inflicting Arcane damage to all players within $74135A2 yards every $74134t1 seconds for $74134d. The amount of Arcane damage dealt changes based on how many Mirror Images were previously destroyed by the players.\n\nNo Mirror Images destroyed: $74135s1 Arcane damage\nOne Mirror Image destroyed: $74366s1 Arcane damage\nTwo Mirror Images destroyed: $74370s1 Arcane damage"},
			{id=2561,title="Celestial Call",body="Isiset summons a number of Celestial Familiars to aid her. The number of Celestial Familiars summoned changes based on how many Mirror Images were previously destroyed by the players.\n\nNo Mirror Images destroyed: One Celestial Familiar\nOne Mirror Image destroyed: Two Celestial Familiars\nTwo Mirror Images destroyed: Three Celestial Familiars"},
			{id=2562,title="Celestial Familiar",body="These floating pieces of stars attack by casting Arcane Barrage at random players."},
			{id=2563,title="Arcane Barrage",body="The Celestial Familiar unleashes a barrage of celestial energy to inflict $74374s1 Arcane damage on a random enemy player."},
			{id=2564,title="Veil of Sky",body="Isiset drapes herself in a protective shield that absorbs damage by draining Isiset's mana instead of her health and reflecting back a percentage of the spells cast at her. The amount of damage absorbed and the chance of a spell being reflected changes based on how many Mirror Images were previously destroyed by the players.\n\nNo Mirror Images destroyed: $74133s1 damage absorbed and $74133s2% chance to reflect spells\nOne Mirror Image destroyed: $74372s1 damage absorbed and $74372s2% chance to reflect spells\nTwo Mirror Images destroyed: $74373s1 damage absorbed and $74373s2% chance to reflect spells"},
		},
	},
	[128]={
		encounterID=128,
		instanceID=70,
		order=5,
		name="Ammunae, Construct of Life",
		lore="Although designed to reduce Azeroth to its base elements, the reordering system inside the Halls of Origination also creates new life. To that end, the construct Ammunae regulates the natural energies coursing through the facility to ensure that life will exist on a reforged Azeroth.",
		dungeonEncounterID=1074,
		uiMapID=299,
		pin={x=0.475,y=0.747},
		difficultyIDs={1,2},
		npcIDs={39731},
		displayIDs={32943},
		loot={
			{itemID=56417,diffs={},faction=-1},
			{itemID=56419,diffs={},faction=-1},
			{itemID=56418,diffs={},faction=-1},
			{itemID=56421,diffs={},faction=-1},
		},
		sections={
			{id=2565,title="Wither",body="Ammunae causes a random player to wither away, reducing their attack and casting speeds by $76043s1% and movement speed by $76043s2% for $76043d."},
			{id=2566,title="Consume Life Energy",body="Ammunae pulls the life and power from a random player, granting himself energy. Consuming the life energy of the player inflicts $79766s2 Nature damage every $79766t2 second and stuns for $79766d. The spell also drains a small amount of either Mana, Runic Power, Rage, Focus, or Energy from the player, depending on their class.\n\nConsuming the life energy grants Ammunae 12 Energy every second for $75665d."},
			{id=2567,title="Seedling Pod",body="Ammunae periodically creates a Seedling Pod in a random location 14 yards away from him. Seedling Pods have low health."},
			{id=2568,title="Energize",body="The Seedling Pod increases Ammunae's damage dealt by $75657s1% and melee haste by $75657s2% while the Pod is alive."},
			{id=2569,title="Energizing Growth",body="The Seedling Pod also heals Ammunae for $89124s1% of his maximum health every $75624t1 seconds while the Pod is alive.",difficultyIDs={2,4,5,6}},
			{id=2570,title="Rampant Growth",body="Ammunae releases all of his stored Life Energy, transforming all Seedling Pods into Bloodpetal Sprouts and inflicting $75790s2 Nature damage to all enemies.\n\nThis spell costs Ammunae 100 Life Energy to cast."},
			{id=2571,title="Bloodpetal Blossom",body="Ammunae infuses a random Seeding Pod with Life Energy, transforming it into a Bloodpetal Blossom."},
			{id=2572,title="Thorn Slash",body="The Bloodpetal Blossom rakes its current target with thorny vines, inflicting $76044s1% of its normal melee damage and causing the target to bleed for $76044s2 Physical damage every $76044t2 seconds for $76044d."},
			{id=2573,title="Spore",body="Ammunae occasionally releases a Spore from his body. This creature moves slowly and has low health. When the Spore dies, it forms a $75702A1 yard radius spore cloud at its location that lasts for 30 seconds."},
			{id=2574,title="Noxious Spores",body="The spore cloud released by the Spore inflicts $75702s1 Nature damage every $75701t1 seconds to any player standing in the cloud. The spore cloud also rots away any plant life inside it, inflicting $75702s2% of the plant's life as Nature damage."},
		},
	},
	[129]={
		encounterID=129,
		instanceID=70,
		order=6,
		name="Setesh, Construct of Destruction",
		lore="Given the purpose of the Halls of Origination, the titans deemed it necessary to create Setesh, a construct who holds sway over the powers of destruction. Should Setesh ever fall to corruption, the results would be disastrous.",
		dungeonEncounterID=1079,
		uiMapID=299,
		pin={x=0.6397,y=0.4925},
		difficultyIDs={1,2},
		npcIDs={39732},
		displayIDs={33055},
		loot={
			{itemID=57871,diffs={},faction=-1},
			{itemID=57874,diffs={},faction=-1},
			{itemID=57873,diffs={},faction=-1},
			{itemID=57872,diffs={},faction=-1},
			{itemID=57875,diffs={},faction=-1},
		},
		sections={
			{id=2666,title="Chaos Bolt",body="Setesh casts Chaos Bolt at random players instead of performing a melee attack. Chaos Bolt inflicts $77069s1 unresistable damage to a random player."},
			{id=2667,title="Reign of Chaos",body="Setesh summons small $77030A2 yard radius bubbles of void energy every $77023t1 second at the location of players and random spots in the room. After a bubble is summoned, it immediately begins to inflict $77030s2 unresistable damage every second to enemies. Each bubble lasts 5 seconds before it pops."},
			{id=2668,title="Chaos Blast",body="Setesh throws a Chaos Blast at the location of a random player that is at least 15 yards away from Setesh. After 5 seconds the Chaos Blast lands at the targeted location, inflicting $76681s1 unresistable damage to any player within $76681A1 yards. The Chaos Blast leaves behind a $76684A1 yard radius void zone that inflicts $76684s1 unresistable damage every second to any player standing in the area."},
			{id=2669,title="Seed of Chaos",body="Setesh creates a Seed of Chaos at a random location in his room that drops to the floor. Moving close to the seed causes it to explode, inflicting $76870s1 Shadow damage to all enemies within $76870A1 yards. Players within the explosion are also infused with chaos for $76870d. and inflict an additional $76874s1 unresistable damage when they land one of their hostile abilities or spells on a target. This additional damage can only occur once every 2 seconds."},
			{id=2670,title="Summon Chaos Portal",body="Setesh channels onto a random location in the room, and opens up a Chaos Portal. When the portal opens, two Void Wurms appear. After another 12 seconds a Void Seeker appears, then after 15 seconds a Void sentinel appears. The Chaos Portal then closes.$[!2,4\n\nIn Heroic Difficulty the Chaos Portal does not automatically close. Players must attack and destroy the portal to stop additional void creatures from entering the fight. When this Chaos Portal opens, a Void Sentinel appears then two Void Wurms appear six seconds later. In another ten seconds a Void Seeker appears. Then every 15 seconds the Chaos Portal is still alive, two Void Wurms or one Void Seeker appears.$]"},
			{id=2671,title="Void Sentinel",body="The Chaos Portal summons one of these very difficult to kill creatures at a time."},
			{id=2672,title="Void Barrier",body="Void Sentinels wrap themselves in a barrier, reducing the damage dealt to them by $76959s1%."},
			{id=2874,title="Charged Fists",body="Void Sentinels charge their fists and increase their Physical damage dealt by $77238s1% and attack speed by $77238s2% for $77238d."},
			{id=2673,title="Void Seeker",body="The Chaos Portal summons one of these void creatures at a time."},
			{id=2674,title="Anti-Magic Prison",body="The Void Seeker channels and traps its current target within an Anti-Magic Prison, reducing their movement speed by $76903s3% and causing the target to become immune to all magical effects (including friendly healing) for $76903d."},
			{id=2675,title="Void Wurm",body="The Chaos Portal summons two of these low health creatures at a time."},
		},
	},
	[130]={
		encounterID=130,
		instanceID=70,
		order=7,
		name="Rajh, Construct of Sun",
		lore="Rajh oversees the energies that have both sparked life and snuffed it out in an untold number of his kin. Considered the mightiest of his fellow constructs, Rajh holds the power to unleash the fury of a thousand suns upon Azeroth.",
		dungeonEncounterID=1078,
		uiMapID=299,
		pin={x=0.475,y=0.253},
		difficultyIDs={1,2},
		npcIDs={39378},
		displayIDs={33177},
		loot={
			{itemID=56429,diffs={},faction=-1},
			{itemID=56436,diffs={},faction=-1},
			{itemID=56427,diffs={},faction=-1},
			{itemID=56434,diffs={},faction=-1},
			{itemID=56433,diffs={},faction=-1},
			{itemID=56428,diffs={},faction=-1},
			{itemID=56435,diffs={},faction=-1},
			{itemID=56431,diffs={},faction=-1},
			{itemID=56430,diffs={},faction=-1},
			{itemID=56432,diffs={},faction=-1},
		},
		sections={
			{id=2926,title="Sun Energy",body="Rajh begins with 100 Sun Energy, and uses this resource to cast his spells."},
			{id=2861,title="Sun Strike",body="Rajh unleashes a burst of flames, inflicting $73872s2 Fire damage to every player within $73872A2 yards and $73874s1 Fire damage every $73874t1 seconds to his current target for $73874d.\n\nThis ability costs Rajh 20 Sun Energy."},
			{id=2862,title="Summon Sun Orb",body="Rajh channels for 3 seconds then summons a Sun Orb above the location of a random player. The Sun Orb then falls, and when it lands the Orb deals $76195s2 Fire damage to any player within $76195A2 yards and knocks them back.\n\nThis ability costs Rajh 20 Sun Energy."},
			{id=2863,title="Inferno Leap",body="Rajh prepares to leap to the location of a random player, then propels himself into the air and lands on the chosen location. While Rajh is casting Inferno Leap, players within $87657A1 yards of the chosen location have their movement speed increased by $87657s1%. When Rajh lands at the chosen location, he inflicts $87647s1 Fire damage and knocks away any player within $87647A1 yards.\n\nThis ability costs Rajh 20 Sun Energy."},
			{id=2864,title="Solar Winds",body="Rajh summons a fiery vortex in front of him. The vortex grows and moves away from Rajh, then begins to move around the room. The Solar Winds vortex inflicts $74108s1 Fire damage and knocks back any players that move within $74108A2 yards.\n\nThis ability costs Rajh 20 Sun Energy."},
			{id=2865,title="Solar Fire",body="As the Solar Winds move across the room, they periodically create small $89133A2 yard patches of Solar Fire. The Solar Fire inflicts $89133s1 Fire damage every $89131t1 second to any player that stands within the flames.",difficultyIDs={2,4,5,6}},
			{id=2866,title="Blessing of the Sun",body="When Rajh has less than 10 Sun Energy, he walks to the middle of the room and reenergizes himself with the Blessing of the Sun for $76355d. Rajh gains 5 Sun Energy, inflicts $76355s3 Fire damage to all players, and increases the damage players inflict by $76355s1% while he channels the Blessing of the Sun."},
		},
	},
