			{itemID=78444,diffs={7},faction=-1},
			{itemID=78847,diffs={5,6},faction=-1},
			{itemID=78919,diffs={3,4,5,6},faction=-1},
			{itemID=78437,diffs={7},faction=-1},
		},
		sections={
			{id=4247,title="Unstable Monstrosity",body="Growing Twilight instability causes arcs of Twilight energy to erupt from Ultraxion's hide. The arcs inflict $%106375s1 Shadow damage every $106372t1 seconds, split evenly amongst enemy players in the Twilight Realm and within $106375A2 yards of the target.\n\nEvery minute that Ultraxion remains in combat reduces the time between arcs by 1 second, to a maximum rate of one arc per second. In addition, the instability prevents Ultraxion from parrying attacks."},
			{id=4248,title="Twilight Shift",body="At the beginning of the battle, Ultraxion pulls all enemies with him into the Twilight Realm where they can bear the full brunt of his powerful Twilight assaults. The Twilight Realm grants players the Heroic Will ability."},
			{id=4249,title="Heroic Will",body="The player's Heroic Will steels the caster's mind to resist the forces of Twilight. This pulls the caster out of the Twilight realm for up to $106108d, but renders them unable to attack, cast spells, or move while concentrating."},
			{id=4250,title="Fading Light",body="Ultraxion sucks the light out of his current target and one random player, drawing them into Twilight over 5-10 seconds. Upon expiration, players in the Twilight Realm instantly die. Players in the normal realm forcibly enter the Twilight Realm, and are afflicted with Faded into Twilight.$[!2,4\n\nIn 25 player Difficulty, Ultraxion sucks the light out of three random players.$]$[!5\n\nIn 10 player Heroic Difficulty, Ultraxion sucks the light out of two random players.$]$[!6\n\nIn 25 player Heroic Difficulty, Ultraxion sucks the light out of six random players.$]$[!7\n\nIn Raid Finder Difficulty, Ultraxion only sucks the light out of his current target.$]"},
			{id=4362,title="Faded into Twilight",body="Residual Twilight effects cause all threat against Ultraxion to be reset. In addition, no threat will be generated for $105927d.$[!5,6\n\nIn Heroic Difficulty, players take $105927s2% more Physical damage for $105927d, instead of generating no threat.$]"},
			{id=4251,title="Hour of Twilight",body="The Hour of Twilight falls upon Ultraxion's foes. Enemies caught within the Twilight Realm take $%103327s1 unresistable Shadow damage. Players within the normal realm forcibly enter the Twilight Realm. If Hour of Twilight does not hit a player, the Aspects take the full brunt of the attack. This disrupts the shield protecting the Aspects and heralds the end of all life on Azeroth.$[!2,4\n\nIn 25 player Normal Difficulty, if Hour of Twilight hits less than three players, the Aspects take the full brunt of the attack.$]$[!5\n\nIn 10 player Heroic Difficulty, if Hour of Twilight hits less than two players, the Aspects take the full brunt of the attack.$]$[!6\n\nIn 25 player Heroic Difficulty, if Hour of Twilight hits less than five players, the Aspects take the full brunt of the attack.$]$[!7\n\nIn Looking for Raid Difficulty, the Aspects can never take the full brunt of the attack.$]",difficultyIDs={1,2,3,4,5,6}},
			{id=4255,title="Looming Darkness",body="When struck by Hour of Twilight, powerful waves of Twilight energy course through the victim, rendering them more susceptible to the harmful effects of Hour of Twilight. Players instantly die if Hour of Twilight inflicts additional damage to them.",difficultyIDs={5,6}},
			{id=4345,title="Hour of Twilight",body="The Hour of Twilight falls upon Ultraxion's foes. Enemies caught within the Twilight Realm take $%103327s1 unresistable Shadow damage. Players within the normal realm forcibly enter the Twilight Realm."},
			{id=4252,title="Twilight Burst",body="If every player stands outside the range of his powerful claws, Ultraxion expels a powerful burst of Twilight energy. This burst inflicts $%106415s1 unresistable Shadow damage on all players and increases their magical damage taken by $106415s2% for $106415d. This effect stacks."},
			{id=4254,title="Twilight Eruption",body="After 6 minutes have passed, Ultraxion's instability reaches uncontainable levels and erupts outwards as a massive explosion that destroys all nearby foes and Ultraxion himself.\n\nIf the shields surrounding the Aspects should fall at any point during the encounter, Ultraxion will immediately trigger Twilight Eruption."},
			{id=4346,title="Protection of the Aspects",body="The Aspects provide limited aid to the players as they fight Ultraxion."},
			{id=4234,title="Alexstrasza"},
			{id=4235,title="Gift of Life",body="Alexstrasza creates a crystal of pure life energy. Activating the crystal imbues one healer with the essence of life itself, increasing healing done by $105896s2% for the duration of the battle. The crystal has one charge. Only one buff granted by Alexstrasza, Ysera, or Kalecgos can be present on a player at any time.$[!4,6,7\n\nIn 25 player raids, Alexstrasza creates two crystals.$]"},
			{id=4236,title="Ysera"},
			{id=4237,title="Essence of Dreams",body="Ysera creates a crystal of dream energy. Activating the crystal imbues one healer with the power of dreams, which causes all healing done to be duplicated and distributed evenly amongst all friendly targets within $105996A2 yards for the remainder of the battle. The crystal has one charge. Only one buff granted by Alexstrasza, Ysera, or Kalecgos can be present on a player at any time.$[!4,6,7\n\nIn 25 player raids, Ysera creates two crystals.$]"},
			{id=4238,title="Kalecgos"},
			{id=4239,title="Source of Magic",body="Kalecgos creates a crystal of amplified arcane energy. Activating the crystal imbues one healer with the essence of magic, reducing the mana cost of all spells by $105903s2% and increasing spell haste by $105903s3% for the remainder of the battle. The crystal has one charge. Only one buff granted by Alexstrasza, Ysera, or Kalecgos can be present on a player at any time.$[!4,6,7\n\nIn 25 player raids, Kalecgos creates two crystals.$]"},
			{id=4240,title="Nozdormu"},
			{id=4241,title="Timeloop",body="Nozdormu captures all players within a finite timeloop.  Any attack which would otherwise kill the player brings them to $105984s2% of maximum health and removes the Timeloop."},
			{id=4242,title="Thrall"},
			{id=4243,title="Last Defender of Azeroth",body="Thrall, now the Earth-Warder of Azeroth, blesses all tanks with the immovable strength of the ancient stones of the world. The blessing reduces defensive cooldowns by $106080s1% and increases defensive ability durations by $106080s2%."},
		},
	},
